            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="SHE12" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>William</forename>
                        <surname>Shelley</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1816-01-24">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1819-06-07"/>
                    <occupation/>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>
    Second child born to Mary Wollstonecraft Shelley and Percy Bysshe Shelley. See his mother's entry in <title>DNB</title>. He died from Malaria in Rome. 
    Godwin records his birth on 24 January 1819: 'william, nepos'. 'Nepos' translates as grandson.
    On 26 June of the same year,  'Letter of nepos', records the letter conveying the news of William's death. 
    It also seems likely that Godwin records a visit from Mary Wollstonecraft Shelley and William in February 1817 before they depart for Marlow.</p>
                        <p>Death recorded in 1819</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="other"><title>DNB</title>.</bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
